.\" Manpage for backend_finder
.TH BACKEND_FINDER 1 "03 August 2026" "v1.0" "Backend API Finder Manual"
.SH NAME
backend_finder \- Machine learning powered application backend and API discovery utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B backend_finder
[\fITARGET_URL\fR]
[\fB\-u\fR \fIURL\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fITHRESHOLD\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-headless\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-color\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B backend_finder
is a command-line security and web-scraping analysis tool designed to identify core backend microservices, REST/GraphQL endpoints, and XHR/Fetch network traffic for any target web application.
.PP
The tool performs static analysis on JavaScript bundle scripts and embedded state tags, followed by live browser network interception using Playwright. Intercepted requests are classified using a Scikit-Learn Machine Learning pipeline (Calibrated Gradient Boosting Classifier, TF-IDF character n-grams, Shannon entropy, and domain affinity features) to score endpoints and filter third-party telemetry, trackers, and static asset noise.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-url " \fIURL\fR"
Target web application URL to inspect (e.g., https://example.com).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Path to write the output JSON report (default: \fIbackend_report.json\fR).
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-threshold " \fITHRESHOLD\fR"
ML confidence score threshold between 0.0 and 1.0 (default: \fI0.50\fR). Requests with scores at or above this threshold are classified as core backend APIs.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-headless
Runs the browser in visible interactive mode instead of headless mode.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose network request tracing output.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI escape sequences for plain-text or piped terminal output.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Basic scan of a web application:
.B backend_finder https://trendyol.com/
.TP
Scan with custom confidence threshold and report output:
.B backend_finder -u https://dummyjson.com/ -t 0.70 -o custom_report.json
.TP
View the manual page:
.B man ./backend_finder.1
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
The output JSON file (\fIbackend_report.json\fR) contains the following sections:
.TP
.B summary
Aggregated counts of captured requests, identified backend APIs, third-party noise, and discovered JavaScript routes.
.TP
.B backend_apis
List of network requests scored at or above the confidence threshold, including HTTP method, URL, resource type, and headers.
.TP
.B js_discovered_endpoints
Endpoints extracted from static JavaScript bundle files ranked by ML confidence score.
.SH FILES
.I backend_finder.py
.RS
Primary Python CLI application executable.
.RE
.I ml_backend_classifier.py
.RS
Scikit-Learn Machine Learning classifier engine.
.RE
.I backend_report.json
.RS
Default output report file.
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR python3 (1),
.BR playwright (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Developed for web scraping, backend auditing, and API discovery workflows.
